  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Fixture masses 12, 22 and 32 kg are illustrative simulated bag properties, not force measurements or a calibrated scale.",
      "The suitcase follows prescribed supported routes. PC derives finite-beam feedback from the actual mesh; PLC owns travel, weighing, route, category result and counters.",
      "Write an infeed / stop-and-weigh / classify-once / discharge sequence. Read weight only with weight_valid. Category thresholds belong in your PLC program.",
      "Stop freezes accepted plant travel and removes local commands. Route changes during discharge are inhibited; the command image remains available for diagnosis.",
      "Load next bag is available only after an exit and with both travel commands off. Change fixture mass before departure. Default ladder remains blank."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is an original functional reference for the control concept, not a copy of the photographed solution.",
      "steps": [
        "Index to bag_at_scale, stop travel and command weigh_cycle with scale_ready.",
        "Classify weight_kg once while weight_valid; increment only the selected category counter.",
        "End weigh_cycle, select the route, discharge to the appropriate exit and stop."
      ],
      "acceptance": "A valid bag produces one category result and increments only its class counter."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [
      "scale/load-cell platform",
      "luggage load",
      "weight display",
      "reject diverter"
    ],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "Supported luggage transport and illustrative fixture-weight feedback. Write PLC logic to weigh each bag, classify it once and increment only its category counter.",
      "startConditions": [
        "The common PLC/watchdog foundation is healthy.",
        "All required simulator inputs are at their documented initial state."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Index to bag_at_scale, stop travel and command weigh_cycle with scale_ready.",
        "Classify weight_kg once while weight_valid; increment only the selected category counter.",
        "End weigh_cycle, select the route, discharge to the appropriate exit and stop."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Stop freezes accepted travel and removes actuator commands. Numeric output images clear; the reference keeps category/counts in PLC memory and republishes them on Run.",
        "Reset restores the home bag, fixture mass and counters."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "Scale ready false invalidates weight; classification waits for a valid dwell.",
        "Conflicting travel/weigh commands and mid-transfer route changes are inhibited without rewriting the PLC image."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "One valid bag yields one category and increments only that class counter when your loaded PLC program implements this logic.",
        "Live weight is the latched fixture mass only while the base is wholly on the weighing deck, weighing is commanded and no travel is commanded.",
        "A completed bag remains visibly on its receiving surface. No contact, calibrated weight or rated mechanism is simulated."
      ]
    },
